      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: \nUseRebootBmcReturn exposes both rebootBmc (the clean action API) and mutation (raw TanStack internal). The view uses mutation.isPending.value and bmcQuery.isError.value directly in the template, bypassing any encapsulation the composable provides.\n\nWhy:\nThis is partially consistent with usePowerControl.ts (which also exposes mutation and metricsQuery), but it creates a pattern where templates are coupled to TanStack Query\u0027s internal ref shapes. If the implementation changes (e.g., moving to a different fetch library), the template must also change. For this PR specifically, mutation.isPending.value could be a derived isBusy: ComputedRef\u003cboolean\u003e in the composable return.\n\nRecommendation:\nConsider exposing derived state instead of raw TanStack objects:\n\n```\nexport interface UseRebootBmcReturn {\n  lastBmcRebootTime: ComputedRef\u003cDate | null\u003e;\n  rebootBmc: () \u003d\u003e Promise\u003cvoid\u003e;\n  isBusy: ComputedRef\u003cboolean\u003e;         // mutation.isPending\n  isError: ComputedRef\u003cboolean\u003e;        // bmcQuery.isError\n  isLoading: ComputedRef\u003cboolean\u003e;      // rootLoading || bmcQuery.isLoading\n}\n```\n\nThis reduces the surface area and isolates TanStack Query from the template layer. (Note: this comment is consistent with the pattern direction already established in this PR but worth raising for future alignment.)",
