      "side": 1,
      "message": "startLoader() is called unconditionally at setup time, followed immediately by a watch with { immediate: true } that calls endLoader() if already not loading (cached re-navigation scenario).\n\nWhy:\nWhen data is already cached (isPageLoading is false at mount), the sequence is:\n\nstartLoader() → emits loader-start\nwatch fires immediately → endLoader() emits loader-end\nBoth fire synchronously before Vue renders. Depending on how AppHeader\u0027s loading bar processes rapid loader-start / loader-end pairs (event counter vs toggle), this may emit unnecessary noise. More importantly, it contradicts the stated goal of \"renders instantly on re-navigation\".\n\nGuard the initial startLoader call:\n\n\nThis makes the intent explicit: start the loader only if there\u0027s actually work to do.",
